23464773875,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":61.8,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.02639380332313479,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":50.6,"_gate_rev_durability":0.22090660728334632,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":100.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0064478952629154545,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":18.3,"_gate_share_shrink":0.0034610414416988977,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":45.7,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.009672945683840842,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":83.9,"_gate_insider_own":0.110319994,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":73.5,"_gate_insider_buying":0.3,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":30.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"SmartFinancial, Inc. operates as the bank holding company for SmartBank that provides various financial services to individuals and corporate customers in the United States. The company offers various deposits, including noninterest-bearing and interest-bearing checking, savings, money market, and individual retirement accounts, as well as certificates of deposit. It also provides commercial and residential real estate, consumer real estate, construction and land development, commercial and industrial, and consumer and other loans, as well as leases to small and mid-size companies for equipment financing leases. In addition, the company offers wealth management, insurance, mortgage origination, and internet and mobile banking services. It operates in Tennessee, Alabama, and Florida. SmartFinancial, Inc. is based in Knoxville, Tennessee.","ceo_bio":"Mr. William Young Carroll Jr. | President, CEO & Director | Age 56 | Compensation: $1.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 581 people. Revenue per employee of $345K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 20%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $102K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["SmartFinancial, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $822M market cap on $200M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years and +22% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 26% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 17-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $59M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 30 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.23\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 0.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.6%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 11% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 59% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Among the least levered in Financial Services \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Why (SMBK) Price Action Is Critical for Tactical Trading","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/21/Why_SMBK_Price_Action_Is_Critical_for_Tactical_Trading_111326025602_1794599762.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794599762.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.557,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Contrasting Byline Bancorp (NYSE:BY) & SmartFinancial (NASDAQ:SMBK)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/10/contrasting-byline-bancorp-nyseby-smartfinancial-nasdaqsmbk.html","date":"2026-11-10","timesta